#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD0004-A expect=violation domain=APMH
#note "DOMAIN carries a well-formed but WRONG four-character AP code. prefix('APMH',4)='APMH' != DOMAIN='APDM' -> fires. Also exercises the split re-test from the other side: the row-0 DOMAIN value 'APDM' differs from the name 'APMH', so the dataset is treated as a split and the Include is satisfied by the NAME leg."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt nameOnly=DOMAIN
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset APMH
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col APID    type=Char
col MHSEQ   type=Num
col MHTERM  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | APDM | AP-001 | 1 | HEADACHE
